<title>BRAZIL: Brazil non-ferrous metals - July statistics.</title>
<headline>Brazil non-ferrous metals - July statistics.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Production in July and consumption, imports and exports of Brazilian non-ferrous metals in January/July compared with 1995 were as follows, said the Secretariat of Mines and Metallurgy.</p>
<p>All figures are in tonnes.</p>
<p>    METAL	    PRODUCTION (JULY)	CONSUMPTION (JAN/JULY)</p>
<p>			  1996	 1995	    1996	 1995</p>
<p> Aluminium	  102,000    101,600	 278,569    325,685</p>
<p> Lead			 0	1,369	     n/a     44,853</p>
<p> Copper		15,613     15,557	 126,267    124,613</p>
<p> Tin		    1,210	1,391	   3,890	2,923</p>
<p> Magnesium		n/a	   41	     n/a	  n/a</p>
<p> Nickel		 1,384	1,391	  11,033     11,148</p>
<p> Zinc		  14,347     18,428	  85,826    120,162</p>
<p> METAL	     EXPORTS (JAN/JULY)	   IMPORTS (JAN/JULY)</p>
<p>			  1996	 1995	    1996	 1995</p>
<p> Aluminium	  486,278    438,661	  48,151     66,759</p>
<p> Lead		   1,511	   94	  16,248     35,786</p>
<p> Copper		43,253     30,530	 856,129    107,548</p>
<p> Tin		    6,444	5,376		26	  149</p>
<p> Magnesium	    1,174	   64	     923	1,677</p>
<p> Nickel		 3,388	2,770	   5,278	4,492</p>
<p> Zinc		  31,369     20,435	   4,349     30,118</p>
<p>-- Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151</p>
</text>
